  "policy": {
    "execution": "Public-entry wall of a fresh instance per entry: Scriptw evaluate entry (Realm bootstrap inside), Porffor exported main (fresh Instance, linear memory and globals), V8 runInContext in a fresh context. Module compilation, native image loading and instantiation are outside the timer.",
    "engines": "Scriptw: precompiled native image on the shared Wasmtime 47.0.0 host, compiler disabled in the consumer. Porffor on Wasmtime: wasmtime-py 47.0.1 compiles the Wasm in-process before timing with the same Cranelift settings (SpeedAndSize, backtracking, explicit x86_64-unknown-linux-gnu target, no host CPU feature inference) and a one-Store pool keeping 16 MiB per memory slot resident; output is captured by a Wasm adapter, the entry is an unchecked ctypes call whose empty-call floor is retained per entry. Porffor on Node/V8: the module is compiled before timing; V8 compiles functions lazily with Liftoff and tiers up to TurboFan during warmups.",
    "v8": "Normal V8 lazy compilation, JIT tiering and natural GC may occur inside entries; ten warmups do not assert steady state.",
